    "_postman_id": "6c1f2e8a-4b7d-4c39-9f0e-2a8d5b3c7e18",
    "name": "Bug Tracker - Notifications and Rate Limit (BTS2-8, BTS2-9)",
    "description": "Notifications (BTS2-8, FR-2) and the write rate limit (BTS2-9, NFR-2). Run the whole collection in order: Auth saves the JWTs into testerToken, devToken and qaToken; the notifications folder creates its own bug (saved to bugId) and checks who is notified at each step.\n\n**Rate limit (NFR-2):** all POST, PATCH and PUT requests under /api are limited to 60 per minute per client IP. Once the limit is reached the API returns 429 with { \"success\": false, \"errors\": [\"Too many requests, please try again in a minute.\"] }. GET requests are not limited. Behind the ALB the client IP comes from X-Forwarded-For (app.set('trust proxy', 1)). Counts are kept per server instance, so with two EC2 instances behind the ALB the effective limit is about 120 per minute: set the instances environment variable to 2 when running through the ALB.\n\nWait at least a minute between full runs, because the rate-limit folder uses up the limit for your IP, and the next run's logins would get 429.\n\nRequires the backend on {{baseUrl}} with the seeded demo users.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
